message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "Ramps and Batteries: why a battery earns what it earns"
abstract: >-
  A two-unit example, small enough to check by hand, showing that a ramp
  constraint rather than a shortage of energy is what pulls two hours apart in
  price, and that the value of storage is the size of that gap. The same reading
  is then applied to a real day of the Brazilian power system, 4 February 2026,
  using open data from the system operator (ONS) and the market chamber (CCEE).
type: software
